      {
        "heading": "How Water's Condition and Location Change the Meaning",
        "content": "The water's condition is the single most important interpretive variable in this dream. Clear, transparent water signals purification, healing, and new beginnings — a positive omen. Murky, polluted, or dark water signals confusion, conflict, and coming difficulty — a warning.\n\nLocation adds another dimension. Rivers represent flow and life transitions: escaping signals resolution, while being trapped warns of prolonged difficulty. The sea represents vast emotional overwhelm and situations that feel beyond personal control. Shallow water softens the warning considerably — the problems you're facing are temporary and likely to resolve with modest help. Deep water amplifies the concern, representing complex, hard-to-escape problems.\n\nA unique note: paradoxically, falling into sewage or waste water is sometimes interpreted in Korean folk tradition as a surprise financial windfall. The same logic applies as in feces dreams — the more unpleasant the sensation, the greater the expected financial gain. It's a counter-intuitive but well-documented folk belief."
