        "heading": "How the Ending Determines Auspicious vs. Warning",
        "content": "In Korean dream interpretation, what happens at the end of a water dream is the decisive factor. The circumstances of falling matter far less than how — or whether — you emerge.\n\nSwimming out under your own power is the strongest positive ending: a symbol of self-directed problem-solving and imminent personal comeback. Being rescued by someone is also positive, foretelling the arrival of a valuable ally or benefactor. Both endings carry the message that difficulties are resolving.\n\nConversely, struggling without escape or drowning is a strong caution — it warns that current difficulties may persist or worsen. In this case, it's worth carefully examining which area of life (health, finances, relationships) needs the most immediate attention."
