    "metaDescription": "What does it mean to dream of a flood in Korean tradition? Clear water means incoming wealth, murky water warns of crisis. Full guide to flood dream symbolism, variations, and cultural context.",
    "h1": "Flood Dream Meaning — The Color of the Water Changes Everything",
    "intro": "A flood dream is one of the most dramatic reversals in Korean dream interpretation — and the single most important detail is the water's clarity. Dream of clean, rushing water flooding your home? That's the dream lottery winners report. Muddy, churning floodwater? The meaning flips 180 degrees. There's one more thing: if you can't remember the water's color, the emotion you felt in the dream holds the answer.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Clear Water Flood Dream — A Major Wealth Omen",
        "content": "In Korean dream tradition, a flood of clean, transparent water ranks among the most auspicious signs you can receive. Water rushing into your home or filling your fields symbolizes wealth literally flowing in — a direct and deeply rooted cultural metaphor. If you run a business, an unexpected major contract or deal may be approaching; if you're an employee, significant good news like a promotion or bonus may be on the way.\n\nMultiple lottery and pension lottery winners in Korea have reported dreaming of their homes flooding with clean water before their winning draw, cementing this dream's reputation as one of the strongest fortune omens in the tradition. The clearer and more abundant the water, the greater the incoming prosperity is believed to be."
