    "h1": "Fog Dream Meaning — The Dream That Splits into Omen and Warning on a Single Detail",
    "intro": "In Korean dream interpretation, a fog dream is rarely neutral. Whether the fog thickens or lifts makes all the difference between a positive omen and a warning — and that single detail is precisely what Korean dream traditions have been tracking for centuries. Historical records from the Joseon Dynasty classified fog by density and color with names like Daemu (大霧), Hwangmu (黃霧), and Heungmu (黑霧), treating it not as weather but as a heavenly sign. So here is the key: if the fog in your dream was clearing, whatever situation feels most opaque in your waking life may be about to open up in ways you cannot yet see.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Understanding Fog Dreams — The Core Symbolism",
