  "en": {
    "title": "Riding a Boat Dream Meaning — Korean Dream Interpretation Guide",
    "metaDescription": "What does riding a boat mean in Korean dream interpretation? Calm sailing signals wealth and promotion; sinking or missing the boat warns of crisis. Full guide with variations.",
    "h1": "Riding a Boat Dream Meaning — What Your Voyage Reveals",
    "intro": "If you dreamed of riding a boat last night, Korean dream tradition has a clear message: a significant turning point in your life is approaching. In 꿈해몽, the boat is not merely a vehicle — it is a powerful archetypal symbol for the course of your fate itself, reflecting the direction and momentum of your life's journey. But here's the crucial detail that most interpretations miss: the exact same boat dream can be a powerful wealth omen or a stark warning of disaster, depending entirely on the condition of the water, the weather, and whether you actually reached your destination.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Auspicious — Calm Sailing, Wealth, and Noble Benefactors",
        "content": "Dreaming of sailing smoothly across calm sea or river waters is one of the most consistently auspicious scenarios in Korean dream interpretation. It signals that you are about to meet a valuable mentor or benefactor who will elevate your social standing, and that success in business or career advancement is on the horizon. A particularly special version: if you see the sun or the moon from the deck of the boat, traditional texts describe this as an omen of repeated honor and career breakthroughs arriving in succession.\n\nDreaming of a boat loaded with goods or jewels arriving at harbor — or of water rising inside the boat itself — is a powerful wealth omen. In Korean folk belief, water symbolizes money and abundance, so water flooding into the hull means wealth is literally flowing into your life. Seeing many ships simultaneously is likewise interpreted as good fortune arriving from multiple unexpected directions at once.\n\nRiding a boat carrying jewels or flying through the sky can be interpreted as a pregnancy dream (태몽) foretelling a remarkable child, or as an omen that a great turning point in destiny is opening up for you. If you dream of becoming the captain and steering the vessel, Korean tradition reads this as a sign that you will soon rise to lead a major organization."
